  "notes": "To successfully deal with and get past a difficulty through effort. Somewhat formal; often used in writing and speeches.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- [obstacle]を{克服|こくふく}する: to overcome [something]\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {困難|こんなん}を{克服|こくふく}する: to overcome difficulties\n- {弱点|じゃくてん}を{克服|こくふく}する: to overcome a weak point\n- {障害|しょうがい}を{克服|こくふく}する: to overcome an obstacle\n- {病気|びょうき}を{克服|こくふく}する: to overcome an illness\n- {恐怖|きょうふ}を{克服|こくふく}する: to conquer fear\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {乗|の}り{越|こ}える: to get over, to overcome (more everyday)\n- {打|う}ち{勝|か}つ: to triumph over (more combative)\n- {克服|こくふく}: noun form (used without する)",
